   "html_text": "His publishing habits also drew attention. Seeking an outlet for longer papers and essays in the late 1970s, and wary of “profiteering” publishers, in the do-it-yourself spirit that infused much of Sylvan’s life he began publishing a number of pre-print series in the Research School of Social Sciences where he worked at the ANU. Beginning with work of the Canberra Logic Group, the “Yellow Series” (as it became known) included over twenty publications by Group members between 1978 and 1985. There",
   "md_text": "His publishing habits also drew attention. Seeking an outlet for longer papers and essays in the late 1970s, and wary of “profiteering” publishers, in the do-it-yourself spirit that infused much of Sylvan’s life he began publishing a number of pre-print series in the Research School of Social Sciences where he worked at the ANU. Beginning with work of the Canberra Logic Group, the “Yellow Series” (as it became known) included over twenty publications by Group members between 1978 and 1985. There"
